{{!-- The identification affordances on an artifact's inventory row (Book I, Discoveries
      pp.430-431). Renders nothing on ordinary gear, so the two column partials can include it
      unconditionally.

      The row's tags/Value and ○ uses were already withheld upstream (see
      concealArtifactFields), so there is nothing to hide HERE: this partial only adds the "?"
      chip that stands in their place, the GM's hint and lead, and the two buttons.

      Both buttons are play actions, not edit ones — the same reasoning that lifted the
      arcanum's "Reveal back" out of edit mode (p.440's ladder can't sit behind the section
      pencil). The GM's is drawn on any `deletable` row (a write-in or a Book II treasure — the
      two kinds of thing that can BE an artifact, as against the playbook's standard kit), so
      there's somewhere to click on a treasure nobody has hidden yet.
      Context: an inventory item snapshot, plus `deletable` from the calling row. --}}
{{!-- The gate also opens on a write-up alone, with no identification state at all. That is the
      resting shape of a Book II treasure now: the book prints a sidebar for the notable ones —
      what it looks like, the custom move it grants — and that text ships on the item
      (data/treasure-catalog.js -> system.artifactLore), whether or not any GM has chosen to
      hide the find. Without this clause the whole block stays folded on an unhidden treasure
      and a player reads the tags and nothing else, which is the gap this all set out to close.
      Every row inside is separately guarded, so nothing else appears any earlier than before. --}}
{{#if (or artifact.isArtifact artifact.lore (and @root.stonetop.isGM deletable))}}
{{#if artifact.concealed}}
<span class="stonetop-inv-artifact-chip{{#if artifact.gmPeeking}} is-gm-peek{{/if}}"
      data-tooltip="{{#if artifact.loreOwed}}{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.chipPartial'}}{{else}}{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.chipUnknown'}}{{/if}}">
	<i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i>
</span>
{{/if}}
{{#if artifact.hint}}
<span class="stonetop-inv-artifact-hint">{{artifact.hint}}</span>
{{/if}}
{{!-- "Once a PC figures an artifact out, give the player its tags, write-up, and any custom
      moves" (p.431). The tags are the note beside the name; this is the write-up. Rendered
      raw — it's GM-authored and declared HTML, exactly like a gear note — with pre-wrap in
      the CSS so a plainly typed one keeps its line breaks. Blank until the state permits it,
      so a still-owed write-up can't leak through the markup. --}}
{{!-- It folds. A treasure's write-up is the book's whole sidebar and a GM's can be as long
      as they please, so the prose hides behind the caret up in the row's icon cluster and the
      row rests at its name and its tags. Shut by default; which rows this user has opened is
      remembered per actor (settings.js -> inventoryLoreExpanded, stamped onto the snapshot as
      `loreExpanded` by the sheet). The caret and the prose sit in ONE wrapper so the fold has
      something to toggle, and that wrapper is boxless (`display: contents`) because the two
      belong to different lines of the row: see the CSS. --}}
{{#if artifact.lore}}
<div class="stonetop-inv-artifact-fold{{#unless artifact.loreExpanded}} is-collapsed{{/unless}}" data-section="{{ownedId}}">
	<a class="stonetop-inv-lore-toggle" role="button" tabindex="0"
	   aria-expanded="{{#if artifact.loreExpanded}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}"
	   aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.loreToggle'}}"
	   data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.loreToggle'}}"><i class="fas fa-caret-down"></i></a>
	<div class="stonetop-inv-artifact-lore{{#if artifact.gmPeeking}} is-gm-peek{{/if}}">{{{artifact.lore}}}</div>
</div>
{{/if}}
{{#if artifact.lead}}
<span class="stonetop-inv-artifact-lead" data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.leadTooltip'}}">
	<i class="fas fa-signs-post"></i> {{artifact.lead}}
</span>
{{/if}}
{{#if artifact.concealed}}
<a class="stonetop-inv-artifact-identify" data-owned-id="{{ownedId}}"
   data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.identifyTooltip'}}">
	<i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass"></i>
</a>
{{/if}}
{{#if @root.stonetop.isGM}}
<a class="stonetop-inv-artifact-gm{{#if artifact.isArtifact}} is-hidden-artifact{{/if}}"
   data-owned-id="{{ownedId}}" data-state="{{artifact.state}}"
   data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.artifact.gmTooltip'}}">
	<i class="fas fa-eye"></i>
</a>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
